'<!-- Section properties of a circular pipe: area, $I_x = I_y = \pi (D^4 - d^4)/64$, section modulus and radii of gyration. -->
"Geometrical Properties of Circular Pipe
'<div style="max-width:150mm"><img style="height:135pt;" alt="circular-pipe.png" class="side" src="../../Images/mechanics/sections/circular-pipe.png"></div>
'Dimensions
d = ? {1}'m,'t = ? {0.1}'m
d_1 = d - 2*t'm
'Area
A = π*(d^2 - d_1^2)/4'm<sup>2</sup>
'Centroid
'<p><i>z</i><sub>c</sub> ='y_c = d/2'm</p>
'Perimeter
P = π*d'm
'Second moments of area
'<p><i>I</i><sub>z</sub> ='I_y = π*(d^4 - d_1^4)/64'm<sup>4</sup></p>
'Polar moment of area
I_x = 2*I_y'm<sup>4</sup>
'Torsional constant
I_t = π*(d^4 - d_1^4)/32'm<sup>4</sup>
'Torsional section modulus
W_t = 2*I_t/d'm<sup>3</sup>
'Radii of gyration
'<p><i>r</i><sub>z</sub> ='r_y = sqrt(I_y/A)'m</p>
r_x = sqr(I_x/A)'m
